title The advisory that had no ceiling -- two GNU-only families gated, and Pond's fixtures made to run on a second bench
prompt The HUSH seat prompt: roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, rota row N mod 5 advancing by hand past a repeat, QA on touch, read scope, ListAgents before a file moves; pick up the running thread and take the next Pond lap under the accrete-only gate boundary. The card and my own last recommend both named the door: the `xargs -r` repair, then `env`.
think THE PEER, NAMED BEFORE A FILE MOVED. ListAgents answered no reachable agents, so ps carried the naming for the fourth lap running. It found a roster already in flight -- pid 380833, thirteen minutes older than mine -- and /proc/380833/cwd read /home/keeper/grain-dream. Dream on its own checkout under ai-jail, me on mine, my index clean throughout. One tree per star holds.
think ROSTER COLD, FORTY-SEVEN MINUTES, AND THE TREE HELD STILL. tree_at_open and tree_at_close both 00595911f7f0, tree_moved=no, host=linux, skipped_host=0, skipped_capability=0. 94 guards, 90 green, 4 red. I read the whole thing before touching a byte. `--scoped` would have been the cheaper open and it REFUSED itself honestly: construction/standing-equipment-receipt.kyri carries digest 1138052a60b8 and no `head` field at all, and the runner refuses a scoped pass without a full receipt carrying a head to diff from. A fusion that cannot prove its delta runs the whole thing, which is the right refusal.
think THE FOUR REDS, ATTRIBUTED RATHER THAN LUMPED. `rule_twin` at 39/36 is custody gate %7 and Keaton's by name. `width_check` is the tree-wide count from another body's lap. `nib_honesty` and `remember_git_nib` are one root -- the card's Git nib naming a commit this repository does not contain -- and both close with the pin riding inside this work commit. So nothing agent-closable stood, and standfast let the lane open.
think ROTA. N=3787 by git rev-list --count HEAD gives row 2, FIRE. The day's own logs record fire read at 03:24 and again at 10:42, three times in all, while row 1 AIR was read once at 05:43 and by nothing since. So I advanced by hand to air, which was both the coldest row and the apt one: air is Saturn, law and boundary, and its question is where does each thing end. Its threshold page gave this lap its test in one sentence -- a claim of a boundary is tested by pressing on it, and if the hand passes through, the boundary was a wish. That is the whole finding below, written a day before I found it.
think THE CARD NAMED ONE LINE AND I PRESSED ON IT RATHER THAN INHERITING IT. My own last recommend said `xargs -r` at pond_enclosure_door_scan.sh:158 is a GNU extension BSD refuses. Before repairing on that word I swept the lane for the whole class, and the sweep is what mattered: four constructs across three files, and then the reading that reframed the lap -- tools/fixtures/s/shell_dialect_scan.sh, rostered and green, was already counting two of them as `advisory_readlink_f=8` and `advisory_sed_i_bare=14`. The guard for this exact class exists, runs every lap, and gates neither number.
think AND THE NUMBERS SAID WHERE THE GROWTH CAME FROM. All 14 of the tree's bare in-place-edit sites stood in two files, both mine: 1 in pond_enclosure_door_control.sh and 13 in pond_policy_launcher_control.sh. The scan's own advisory comment records five sites measured 20260826.090745. So the family grew from five to fourteen in three days, entirely inside the one lane whose two guards were redding on the macOS bench across at least two laps, logged there in a peer's own words as two Pond guards that red on a macOS bench.
think THE PROMOTION CONDITION WAS ALREADY WRITTEN, AND NOBODY WAS THE READER. tools/s/shell_dialect_witness.rish's header says a family earns its gate by costing a real reading on a real host, and the two still advisory are reported until they do. Both had cost one. That sentence is a promotion condition living in prose, checked by whoever happens to read the header -- which is the same shape as the launcher's uid warning I turned into a checked thing one lap ago, and the same shape as %329. A note somebody hopes is read against a thing a program checks.
think THE ASYMMETRY IS THE PART WORTH SAYING, so I measured it rather than assuming both families deserved the same treatment. In-place edit: 14 sites, all repairable, all mine -- so a hard gate at ZERO. Resolve flag: 8 sites, of which FIVE are shell_portable_control.sh calling the elder spelling on purpose to compare resolve_path against it, each behind a `have_rl` probe that says out loud when it skips, and a sixth is tools/ag/agent-jail.sh, which my own accrete-only gate boundary forbids me to touch. That family can honestly reach two and no further today, so it takes a RATCHET at seven rather than a gate at zero. A ceiling of zero there would name a number no edit in this tree is allowed to reach.
obs THE NAMED LINE CARRIED A SECOND FAULT, AND THAT ONE I COULD PROVE HERE. The card asked about portability, which needs a Mac I do not have. But `| head -1 | xargs -r dirname` also WORD-SPLITS: measured in a pen on this pier, a persist path of `/home/user/my pier/loops/claude` came back through xargs as TWO lines, `/home/user` and `pier/loops`, where the quoted form answers `/home/user/my pier/loops` correctly. record_home is the namespace every later path comparison is measured against, so a wrong one is wrong everywhere at once. Honest bound on it: this is the FALLBACK leg, latent while the rw-map line above answers on the living record. Latent rather than active, and free to repair.
obs THE TWO NEWLINE PLANTS WERE THE SHARPEST FAULT AND I ALMOST MISSED THEM. Two of the thirteen launcher-control sites put `\n` in an s/// replacement, which GNU sed reads as a newline and BSD sed reads as the letter n. Those two plants build the pens for cases 9 through 13. On a BSD bench they would not have ERRORED -- they would have planted the wrong text and let the case pass or fail for the wrong reason, which is exactly the vacuous pass this whole family was booked for. Repaired with `&` plus a backslash-escaped literal newline, proven byte-identical against the elder spelling in a pen before I touched the tree, and proven again afterward by the control: `a mount the record never declared refuses` still passes, which it can only do if the line really got inserted.
obs THE EQUIVALENCE WAS MEASURED, NOT ASSERTED. resolve_path against readlink -f on the real value this scan resolves: both answered /nix/store/2m6ixmpspk7qm5g3j4vnlyb7bjxqpslw-claude-code-2.1.235/bin/claude, and both answered empty on empty input. The door witness then read entry_state=declared entry_unreachable=0 on metal after the swap, which is the same reading it gave before.
obs WHAT THE ACCRETE-ONLY BOUNDARY COST ME, AND IT WAS THE RIGHT COST. One of the eight resolve-flag sites is tools/ag/agent-jail.sh. Repairing it would have taken the family to six and looked tidier. It is the launcher, every markdown that instructs a reader about it stands untouched until the switchover lands behind its audit, and a fixture repair is not the switchover. So it stays, the ceiling is seven rather than six, and the reason is written into the guard's own comment where the next reader meets it rather than into a log nobody greps.
obs I DECLINED TO ADD AN EXEMPTION THAT WOULD HAVE LOOKED BETTER. The scan already skips two files that spell these idioms on purpose -- itself and the helper. Adding shell_portable_control.sh as a third would have dropped the resolve-flag reading from seven to two and made the ceiling look almost closed. I left it counted: a gate that grows an exemption stops being a gate, and the honest number with its five structural sites NAMED in the comment teaches more than a flattering one.
obs A CLAIM I COULD NOT SETTLE, NAMED AS THE FALSIFIER RATHER THAN SMOOTHED. I have no macOS bench, so I cannot show that these constructs are what redden those two Pond guards there. What I have is: two guards red there, their fixtures carry the tree's entire population of one GNU-only family, and this tree already gated four sibling families for costing exactly this kind of reading. That is an inference, and the Mac's next run is what settles it. The row says so on its face.
obs THE CARD HAD ELEVEN BYTES FREE, SO THE UPDATE PAID FOR ITSELF. construction/ITINERARY.md stood at 24,565 of 24,576. My new paragraph cost 26 bytes net after folding the two landed Pond paragraphs -- the door duty and the capability tier, both of which have their own logs -- and tightening the still-open and next-doors blocks paid another 142 back. The card closes at 24,449 with 127 free.
obs THE HEADLINE WAS DERIVED AND MY ROW MOVED IT, WHICH THE WITNESS CAUGHT RATHER THAN ME. reds_ledger_monotone refused with headline remainder 329 against the derived 330, and reds_ledger_headline_write.sh repaired it in one call. The pin closes at 16,614 of 24,576 with 6 rows, 1 OPEN (%349, Mind's own handback), 5 foldable, pin_deadlocked=0. Booking was possible this lap for the first time in five -- the four before it declined for want of room.
obs QA ON TOUCH, FIVE PROGRAMS AT METER: both Pond controls, the door scan, the dialect scan, and the dialect witness. Every one composite 94, letter A, truth 100 with all cited paths resolving. No frame pushed.
obs THE HOT PASS EARNED ITS PLACE AGAIN, AND THE RED IT FOUND WAS NOT MINE. The cold open read witness_reach GREEN; the hot pass over the staged tree read it RED at wholly_unreached=221 against a family ceiling of 220. Between the two I had fast-forwarded seven upstream commits, and one of them -- 9d1df6b3d2, a peer's lantern-face lap landed six minutes before my own stamp -- added tools/l/lantern_face_witness.rish with no roster row beside it. A witness nothing enumerates is a family with no clock. The guard's own refusal names the repair rather than leaving it to taste: give it a roster row rather than raise the ceiling.
obs I CLOSED IT RATHER THAN SURFACING IT, because it is a POND witness and Pond is my lane -- and I checked it was safe to roster before rostering it, since a row for an unstable witness would red my own tree on every lap after. It runs GREEN in 9.5s measured here, which is `tier lap`. wholly_unreached fell 221 -> 220, standing rose 213 -> 214, and the roster parses at 113 rostered with zero path-missing, zero half-written, zero unknown tier. That is the OPPOSITE call from the session-logs pin one screen up, and the difference is the whole test: the pin is a peer's live room with their own commits landing in it this hour, while a missing roster row for a Pond guard is my lane's own gap and additive to their work rather than over it.
